ass=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nuwisha Nutjob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/524092-confused-about-tooth-and-claw#post524092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit confused. On page 186 of WtF 2Ed, under the title Tooth and Claw, it talks about how werewolves can deal devestating damage to a weaker spirit because of their Rank. Ok, makes sense. But then it says that a high ranking spirit can't damage a Uratha in turn just by touching it. So is this implying that spirits can't hurt Uratha at all directly? Because I thought that spirits could inflict damage on a Uratha? Did I miss something?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means that spirits of significantly higher rank than Uratha do not pose the same threat that they, themselves pose to spirits. At that point, spirits have other alternatives than sheer food chain predominance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}